[h1]FPS Map – Calm Water Add-on[/h1]

[b]An optional add-on for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3828926440]FPS Map – Updated for 1.19[/url] that tones down the bright sun glare on the sea.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What it does[/h2]
At mid zoom, the sun draws a large bright white spot on the sea that moves with the camera. This add-on scales only the sun's specular light on water to 35%:
[list]
[*]Water colour, waves, sea ice, borders and map modes — unchanged.
[*]One line differs from the 1.19.4 water shader; everything else is the current vanilla file.
[/list]

[h2]⚠ Not for Millennium Dawn[/h2]
Millennium Dawn ships its own water shader (it removes the water darkening and the sea gradient borders). This add-on would replace it and undo those MD changes — [b]don't enable both[/b]. FPS Map itself stays fully compatible with MD.

[h2]Installation[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3828926440]FPS Map – Updated for 1.19[/url] (required).
[*]Subscribe to this add-on and enable both — the launcher loads it after FPS Map automatically.
[/olist]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Purely visual: [b]Ironman and multiplayer safe[/b] (game checksum unchanged, verified in game), add or remove at any time. Works together with the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3828959483]Colour-blind Add-on[/url].
